    "type": "question",
    "label": "25",
    "prompt": "Find the equation of the line with $x$-intercept 6 and $y$-intercept 11.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$11x+6y=66$.",
      "worked": "The intercepts give the points $(6,0)$ and $(0,11)$.\n$$\\begin{align*}m&=\\frac{0-11}{6-0}\\\\m&=-\\frac{11}{6}\\end{align*}$$\nUsing $(0,11)$:\n$$\\begin{align*}y-11&=-\\frac{11}{6}(x-0)\\\\y&=-\\frac{11}{6}x+11\\\\6y&=-11x+66\\\\11x+6y&=66\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
